OL,3,GNEWSAFamilies separated by 2,000 miles
OL,4,Ahelp track down tiny science boat
OL,5,
OL,6,FA schoolboy in the Western Isles has
OL,7,Ffound a tiny sail boat which has spent
OL,8,F15 months crossing 2,000 miles of the
OL,9,FAtlantic.
OL,11,FThe craft, which is fitted with a GPS
OL,12,Ftracker, was launched in June last year
OL,13,Ffrom Portland, Maine, in the US, as
OL,14,Fpart of a science project.
OL,16,FShortly afterwards, it came ashore in
OL,17,FNewfoundland, Canada. It was put to sea
OL,18,Fagain in June this year by a school
OL,19,Fattended by the daughter of Gemma
OL,20,FMacKinnon, who is originally from the
OL,21,Fisles.
OL,23,APub: 29-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB  Scot NewsC Reg TVF  Weather
FL,428,420,260,160,0,100
